.TITLE "open"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Opens files, directories, and applications using their default macOS applications.
It can also open URLs in the default web browser and execute scripts or commands.
This command is a versatile utility for interacting with the graphical environment
from the command line.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**start**

.DIV "TLDR"
**open .**
Opens the current directory in Finder.
> 

**open __file.txt__**
Opens a __file.txt__ with its default application.
> __file.txt__: The path to the file to open.

**open -a "__Application Name__" __file.txt__**
Opens a __file.txt__ with a specific "__Application Name__".
> __Application Name__: The name of the application to use. | __file.txt__: The path to the file to open.

**open __https://www.example.com__**
Opens a URL in the default web browser.
> __https://www.example.com__: The URL to open.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The `open` command simplifies launching applications and viewing files from
the terminal. It respects the macOS association of file types with specific
applications, providing a seamless bridge between the command line and GUI.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:mdfind**

